{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1842","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"H. Tenzing and Random Real Numbers"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1024 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are $$$n$$$ uniform random real variables between 0 and 1, inclusive, which are denoted as $$$x_1, x_2, \\ldots, x_n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Tenzing has $$$m$$$ conditions. Each condition has the form of $$$x_i+x_j\\le 1$$$ or $$$x_i+x_j\\ge 1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Tenzing wants to know the probability that all the conditions are satisfied, modulo $$$998~244~353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Formally, let $$$M = 998~244~353$$$. It can be shown that the answer can be expressed as an irreducible fraction $$$\\frac{p}{q}$$$, where $$$p$$$ and $$$q$$$ are integers and $$$q \\not \\equiv 0 \\pmod{M}$$$. Output the integer equal to $$$p \\cdot q^{-1} \\bmod M$$$. In other words, output the integer $$$x$$$ that $$$0 \\le x \\lt M$$$ and $$$x \\cdot q \\equiv p \\pmod{M}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$m$$$ ($$$1\\le n\\le 20$$$, $$$0\\le m\\le n^2+n$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Then following $$$m$$$ lines of input contains three integers $$$t$$$, $$$i$$$ and $$$j$$$ ($$$t \\in \\{0,1\\}$$$, $$$1\\le i\\le j\\le n$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If $$$t=0$$$, the condition is $$$x_i+x_j\\le 1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" If $$$t=1$$$, the condition is $$$x_i+x_j\\ge 1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that all conditions are pairwise distinct."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output the probability that all the conditions are satisfied, modulo $$$M = 998~244~353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 2\n0 1 2\n1 3 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n748683265\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 3\n0 1 2\n0 1 3\n0 2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n748683265\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 4\n0 1 2\n0 1 3\n1 2 3\n1 2 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n935854081\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 4\n0 1 2\n0 3 4\n1 1 3\n1 2 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n8 12\n0 1 2\n0 2 3\n1 3 4\n0 1 4\n0 5 6\n0 6 7\n1 7 8\n0 5 8\n1 3 7\n1 3 8\n1 4 7\n1 4 8\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n997687297\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, the conditions are $$$x_1+x_2 \\le 1$$$ and $$$x_3+x_3\\ge 1$$$, and the probability that each condition is satisfied is $$$\\frac 12$$$, so the probability that they are both satisfied is $$$\\frac 12\\cdot \\frac 12=\\frac 14$$$, modulo $$$998~244~353$$$ is equal to $$$748683265$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, the answer is $$$\\frac 14$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, the answer is $$$\\frac 1{16}$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the fourth test case, the sum of all variables must equal $$$2$$$, so the probability is $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"H","problemCode":"1842H","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1842/problem/H"}